## Claim amendment · step 1 accepted · 2026-11-09T03:21Z

This amends the claim on #30514, after the dev's step-1 report 6731426750 (`premise_still_valid: true`).

- **Option A, land now.** The menu offers the app's list read through `resolveBuiltInLanguage`:
  - kept only where it lands on a table tag;
  - de-duplicated;
  - in the app's declared order;
  - as table tags.
  The `provisional` self-heal is judged against the offered set. The loader's credit in `canResolveLanguage` is retired in the same PR, and the checkmark compares through the same resolution. An empty intersection keeps today's offline fallback.
  - **Why now, not `Blocked-by` the backfills:** the Studio namespace (2 of 11) and built-in emails (4 of 11) are incomplete today, whatever this card does. A reads the same list and only removes entries, so it adds no language anywhere. Ruling F is already met for what A offers on the Console packs, marketplace and server bundles, as measured.
- **Surface widened by one file:** `ui/apps/console/src/pages/system/ProfilePage.tsx` (~L639–646). The stored-value check matches through the same resolution, so an account storing `zh-CN` sees one 简体中文 option, not a stray 中文（中国）.
- **Declarations, replacing the claim's:** `Clause-②: no (narrowing)`, `Metadata-protocol: none`.
  - Narrowing: an app locale with no table tag (for example `th`), offered today, is no longer offered. First-party apps affected: **0**. Every first-party declaration (app-crm, app-showcase, app-todo, HotCRM sales) uses read aliases, and all of them land on table tags.
  - The ruling F intersection is the maintainer's own rule, so it needs no further decision. A `CONTRACT_REVIEW_TIER` review is owed before the queue; the seat requests it at PR time. The PR body carries the measured case table and the 0-app census.
- **Tests at build:**
  - the four alias cases (2b–2d, 4a) read as table entries with table labels, and 4a is one entry;
  - `th` is dropped, and a stored `th` is purged once the list lands;
  - CONTROL: case 1 (no loader) offers the 11 table tags as today;
  - the ProfilePage case;
  - the rewritten `provider-app-locale-restore` `th` cases;
  - ablation of the canonicalizing step.
- **Out-of-scope findings:** a (the Studio namespace, 2 of 11, with zh-Hant resolving to Simplified), b (built-in emails, 4 of 11) and c (`TranslationConfigSchema` accepts an out-of-table `supportedLocales` entry). All three are carried on the ruling F tracking card #29428, which owns "complete on every surface". The seat files no separate cards (one close-out card per family).
